  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Establishment of Local Language/FoRB Center in Chennai</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The central purpose of this project is to combat the rising instances of Freedom of Religion or Belief (FoRB) violations faced by North Indian migrants living in Chennai.
Participants:
50 adult North Indian migrants (male and female, ages 18&#x2013;45),
20 children (ages 5&#x2013;15) from migrant families.
Activities:
Establishment of a dedicated Language and Freedom of Religion or Belief (FoRB) Education Center, envisioned as a transformative space for linguistic empowerment, rights education, and social integration for North Indian migrants living in Chennai.
Expected outcome
At least 70% of adult participants demonstrate improved Tamil proficiency (based on pre/post assessments).
80% of participants report increased knowledge of legal rights and mechanisms for redress.
Number of FoRB violations documented and reported by trained CBOs increases by 50%.</narrative>
  </description>
